     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin and segmented true, and all other defence constants false, the attacker can reach: exploit_web giving foothold_web; phish_workstation giving foothold_workstation and stolen_user; escalate_workstation giving admin_workstation; pivot_internal, since admin_workstation satisfies the segmented condition, giving reach_internal; auth_appserver giving foothold_appserver; kerberoast_dc giving stolen_admin; and escalate_appserver giving admin_appserver. However, auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, which the deployed MFA defence blocks. So foothold_dc, admin_dc and stolen_dbadmin can never be obtained, because dump_dbadmin_dc is the only source of stolen_dbadmin. Without stolen_dbadmin, neither auth_db nor auth_fileserver can fire. That leaves no foothold or admin on the db or fileserver, so neither exfiltrate_db nor exfiltrate_fileserver is reachable.\"}"
